      "title": "p4rpc: Fixup truncation",
      "message": "p4rpc: Fixup truncation\n\nDon't call ws_utf8_truncate unless we wrote to the end of the buffer\n(and thus there's possibly a truncated UTF-8 codepoint); this prevents\nUB with the end of the string buffer not being initialized.\n\nThis shows a reason why snprintf is tricky, remembering which parameters\ninclude the null terminator and which ones don't.\n\nFix #20922 (while keeping #20916 fixed.)\n",
      "author_name": "John Thacker",
      "author_email": "johnthacker@gmail.com",
